Trailers
Signed-off-by: Ada Desk &lt;ada@example.com&gt;
Co-authored-by: Sam Desk &lt;sam@example.com&gt;
Fixes: #18
git interpret-trailers reads these. Signed-off-by is a project convention (Linux kernel, some forges). Use it when the project asks. Co-authored-by is how forges attribute a second author on a squash.

Label it in the message
git cherry-pick -x &lt;hash&gt;
-x appends (cherry picked from commit …) to the message. Useful on release branches so git log shows the origin hash.

Named and multiple
git stash push -m "experiment A"
git stash push -m "experiment B"
git stash list
git stash apply stash@{1}
git stash drop stash@{1}
git stash show -p stash@{0}
Numbers shift when you drop. The message is how you find them.
